  "abstract": {
    "value": "The excessive accumulation of nitrate/nitrite (NO <sub><i>x</i></sub> <sup>-</sup>) in surface and groundwater has severely disrupted the global nitrogen cycle and jeopardized public health. The electrochemical conversion of NO <sub><i>x</i></sub> <sup>-</sup> to ammonia (NH<sub>3</sub>) not only holds promise for ecofriendly NO <sub><i>x</i></sub> <sup>-</sup> removal, but also provides a green alternative to the energy-intensive Haber-Bosch process for NH<sub>3</sub> production. Recently, in addition to the electrocatalyst design explosion in this field, many innovative valorization systems based on NO <sub><i>x</i></sub> <sup>-</sup>-to-NH<sub>3</sub> conversion have been developed for generating energy and expanding the range of value-added products. Collective knowledge of advanced conversion systems is indispensable for restoring the global nitrogen cycle and promoting a N-based economy. Herein, a timely and comprehensive review is provided on the important progress of valorization systems based on NO <sub><i>x</i></sub> <sup>-</sup> conversion, including waste treatment systems, novel electrolytic systems, and energy conversion and storage systems. Some mechanism exploration",
    "source": "external_discovery",
    "confidence": 0.98,
    "human_checked": false
  },
